  "pli-tv-bu-vb-np6:2.14": "“A communal robe” renders <i lang='pi' translate='no'>vihāracīvara</i>, literally, “a dwelling robe”. Since “dwelling robe” is awkward in English, and because these robes did not belong to individual monastics, I prefer the given rendering. “A bedspread” renders <i lang='pi' translate='no'>uttarattharaṇa</i>. Sp 1.517: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Uttarattharaṇanti mañcakassa upari attharaṇakaṁ vuccati</i>, “What is spread on top of a bed is called an <i lang='pi' translate='no'>uttarattharaṇa</i>.” ",
