  "pli-tv-bu-vb-np6:3.1.6": "For an explanation of this, see comment at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/pli-tv-bu-vb-np4/en/brahmali#2.1.6'>Bu NP 4:2.1.6</a>. ",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-np6:3.1.7": "",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-np6:3.1.8": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Agāraṁ</i> is typically rendered as “in a house”. The problem with this is that it is not unallowable for a monastic to live in a building that is the equivalent of a house. What a monastic should not do is own a home and then live there. ",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-np6:3.1.9": "",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-np6:3.1.10": "",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-np6:3.1.11": "",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-np6:3.1.12": "The six are linen, cotton, silk, wool, sunn hemp, and hemp; see <a href='https://suttacentral.net/pli-tv-kd8/en/brahmali#3.1.6'>Kd 8:3.1.6</a>. According to <a href='https://suttacentral.net/pli-tv-kd8/en/brahmali#21.1.4'>Kd 8:21.1.4</a>, the size referred to here is no smaller than 8 by 4 <i lang='pi' translate='no'>sugataṅgula</i>, “standard fingerbreadths”. For an explanation of the idea of <i lang='pi' translate='no'>vikappanā</i>, see Appendix of Technical Terms. For the rendering of <i lang='pi' translate='no'>cīvara</i> as “robe-cloth”, see the same appendix. ",
